1508-/**Function*************************************************************
1509-
1510-  Synopsis    [Returns 1 if a fanout/load proxy should reject this cut.]
1511-
1512-  Description [Mode 1 is the classic map -f guard. Mode 2 is the stmap1
1513-  selective guard, which only rejects wider cuts when the node has higher
1514-  estimated fanout. Mode 3 is the stmap2 guard, which uses the same fanout
1515-  thresholds only during area recovery and only when the current phase has
1516-  slack over the mapper required time. Mode 4 is the stmap3 guard, which
1517-  narrows the intervention to high-fanout nodes with only shallow positive
1518-  slack. Mode 5 is the stmap4 split-phase guard: stmap1-style guarding in
1519-  delay matching and stmap2-style slack-aware guarding in area recovery.
1520-  Mode 6 is the stmap5 shape-gated split-phase guard: the delay pass only
1521-  uses stmap1-style guarding in very large mapper graphs, while area recovery
1522-  keeps the stmap2 slack-aware guard. Mode 7 is the stmap6 area-sensitive
1523-  shape-gated guard: the delay pass keeps the stmap5 graph-size gate, small
1524-  mapper graphs keep the stmap2 slack-aware recovery guard, and exact-area
1525-  recovery on larger graphs checks the cut after matching so materially cheaper
1526-  cuts can override the fanout/load proxy. Mode 8 is the stmap7 criticality-
1527-  sensitive version of mode 7: exact-area recovery on larger graphs allows the
1528-  override only with deeper mapper slack and outside the highest fanout bucket.
1529-  Mode 9 is the stmap8 arrival-bounded version of mode 8: the area-saving
1530-  override also requires the candidate match to stay within one quarter of an
1531-  inverter delay of the existing mapper arrival. Mode 10 is the stmap9
1532-  middle-slack area-relief version of mode 9: it keeps the highest fanout
1533-  bucket protected, but in the one-to-two inverter slack bucket it allows a
1534-  wide cut only when it is arrival-neutral and saves at least one inverter
1535-  area. Mode 11 is the stmap10 depth-qualified version of mode 10: the
1536-  middle-slack relief is allowed only for shallow and medium-depth nodes.
1537-  Mode 12 is the stmap11 tight-depth version of mode 11: the middle-slack
1538-  relief is allowed only for shallower nodes. Mode 13 is the stmap12
1539-  fanout-bucket split version of mode 12: the tight-depth middle-slack relief
1540-  is allowed only in the lower moderate fanout bucket. Mode 14 is stmap13,
1541-  which keeps mode 13 behavior while recording guard-hit counters. Mode 15 is
1542-  stmap14, which keeps the same bucket and counters but requires a stronger
1543-  middle-slack area-flow saving. Mode 16 is stmap15, which restores the
1544-  one-inverter relief threshold only after the current run has observed a high
1545-  lower-moderate/middle-slack exact-area profile. Mode 17 is stmap16, which
1546-  keeps mode 16 behavior and prints per-relief diagnostics. Mode 18 is stmap17,
1547-  which uses the one-inverter post-profile threshold only for candidates with
1548-  materially better mapper arrival. Mode 19 is stmap18, which keeps mode 18
1549-  decisions and adds near-miss diagnostics for candidates rejected by the
1550-  timing-quality/profile fallback. Mode 20 is stmap19, which allows the
1551-  one-inverter threshold before profile-open only for candidates with the same
1552-  material mapper-arrival improvement. Mode 21 is stmap20, which keeps the
1553-  mode 20 pre-profile seed but restricts it to shallow nodes. Mode 22 is
1554-  stmap21, which keeps the shallow seed and admits deeper pre-profile seeds
1555-  only when the arrival gain is unusually large. Mode 23 is stmap22, which
1556-  relaxes the deep pre-profile seed boundary to a moderate arrival gain. Mode
1557-  24 is stmap23, which keeps the strong deep seeds but allows moderate deep
1558-  seeds only when the existing mapper slack is near the critical side of the
1559-  middle-slack window. Mode 25 is stmap24, which tightens the moderate deep
--
