The stmap45 mode does not consistently enforce its advertised pressure-agreement admission rule, allowing a class of soft seeds to bypass the pressure check and receive the lighter area margin.

Review comment:

- [P2] Enforce pressure agreement for all soft seeds — /Users/cunxiy/Documents/research/autoresearch-eda/abc-harness/src/map/mapper/mapperMatch.c:2303-2305
  For mode 46, this only consults pressure through `Stmap45ModeratePenaltyFactor` when `fStmap45ModeratePenaltyCandidate` is true. If a soft seed is admitted through the tight-critical branch (`Map_MatchHasStmap28SoftPenaltyModerateDeepSeed()` true but `fStmap45ModeratePenaltyCandidate` false), `fStrictFallback` becomes false without checking node/cut pressure, so a no-pressure candidate can still use the one-inverter margin that stmap45 is supposed to reserve for pressure agreement.
